PathLab is an independent implementation by Issac Johny.
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Andrew F. Hayes or PROCESS.
No PROCESS implementation, manual or original template artwork is included.
The original PathLab icon illustrates the conceptual structure commonly called
PROCESS Model 59: X -> M -> Y and X -> Y, with W moderation of all three
paths. Its shapes are unfilled, with colored outlines and letters.
It is branding, not a model preset or active graph.

Dependencies retain their own licenses. The tested jamovi runtime provides
jmvcore (GPL >= 2), R6 (MIT), jsonlite (MIT), digest (GPL >= 2), and R base
packages (R GPL >= 2 distribution). These dependencies are not relicensed here.
Bundled numerical examples and datasets are synthetic; they contain no research
participants' records. Statistical methods and limitations are in METHODS.md.
